  "database": "rschema_0425",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0425 database is designed to manage various aspects of a residential facility, including user information, building details, announcements, dormitory management, student records, maintenance records, and applications. At the core of the database is the User table, which stores information about individuals with unique User IDs, usernames, and passwords, as well as their roles within the facility. Each user can be assigned to a role, and users with the role of dormitory supervisor are linked to specific buildings through the Building table, which contains details such as the building's name, location, and type. The Building table also references the User table to establish the relationship between the dormitory supervisor and the building they oversee. The Announcement table stores announcements made by users, including the announcement's title, content, and release time, and is linked to the User table to identify the administrator who made the announcement. The Dormitory table contains information about each dormitory, including its name, facilities, number of beds, and type, and is linked to the Building table to establish the relationship between the dormitory and the building it is located in. The Student table stores information about students, including their name, class, gender, and dormitory ID, and is linked to the Dormitory table to establish the relationship between the student and their assigned dormitory. The Maintenance_Record table stores maintenance records, including the completion time, fault description, maintenance status, and report time, and is linked to the Dormitory table to identify the dormitory where the maintenance was performed and the User table to identify the maintenance staff member. Finally, the Application table stores applications made by students, including the application content, application time, application type, processing opinion, and processing status, and is linked to the Student table to establish the relationship between the student and their application.",
  "gold_question": "The student dormitory management system business requirement description:\nA student dormitory management system includes functions such as user management, building management, dormitory management, and student management. The system has users with different roles, such as administrators, dormitory managers, students, and maintenance staff. Each user has a unique ID, username, and password. Building information includes building ID, name, type, location, description, and the responsible dormitory manager. Dormitory information includes dormitory ID, name, type, number of beds, belonging building, supporting facilities, and the responsible dormitory manager. Student information includes student ID, name, gender, belonging dormitory, class, etc. Students can submit various applications (bed change, repair, absence registration, check-out application, etc.). The system records application ID, application type, applicant student ID, application content, application time, application status, and administrator's processing opinion. Administrators can process these applications, review and approve or reject them. Dormitory managers can handle students' leave and repair applications, and manage absence registration. Maintenance staff can handle repair applications and record maintenance information. Maintenance records include maintenance record ID, dormitory ID, fault description, repair time, maintenance staff ID, maintenance situation, and completion time. The system also includes announcement management for administrators to publish and manage announcement information. Announcement information includes announcement ID, announcement title, announcement content, release time, and the ID of the administrator who released the announcement.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0425.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0425\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `building` (\n  `building_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `supervisor_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`building_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `building_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`supervisor_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `announcement` (\n  `announcement_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `release_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`announcement_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `announcement_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`admin_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `dormitory` (\n  `dormitory_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `facilities` text NOT NULL,\n  `number_of_beds` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `building_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`dormitory_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `dormitory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`building_id`) REFERENCES `building` (`building_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `student` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `class` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `dormitory_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`dormitory_id`) REFERENCES `dormitory` (`dormitory_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `maintenance_record` (\n  `maintenance_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `completion_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `fault_description` text NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `report_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `dormitory_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`maintenance_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `maintenance_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`dormitory_id`) REFERENCES `dormitory` (`dormitory_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `maintenance_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `application` (\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `application_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `application_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `processing_opinion` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `processing_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`application_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `application_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
